---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ShareAnchor from "@/components/react/ShareAnchor";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why Pregnancy, Clearly exists and what it intentionally does not do."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">About the project</p><h1>
        Information that respects<br />the person reading it.
      </h1><p class="lede">
        Pregnancy, Clearly is built for the moment when every tab seems either
        frightening, patronizing, commercial or too vague to use.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="reading-shell article-stack">
      <section
        class="content-section"
        id="what-it-is"
        data-share-target
        tabindex="-1"
      >
        <ShareAnchor targetId="what-it-is" label="what this guide is" />
        <h2>What it is</h2><p>
          A static, fast and private guide to the nine months of pregnancy,
          designed especially for first-time parents and the people supporting
          them. An after-birth continuation is available when it becomes useful.
        </p>
      </section><section
        class="content-section"
        id="what-it-is-not"
        data-share-target
        tabindex="-1"
      >
        <ShareAnchor targetId="what-it-is-not" label="what this guide is not" />
        <h2>What it is not</h2><p>
          It is not a clinic, symptom checker, diagnostic tool, personalized
          treatment plan, forum, shopping guide or advertising platform.
        </p>
      </section><section
        class="content-section"
        id="why-it-feels-different"
        data-share-target
        tabindex="-1"
      >
        <ShareAnchor
          targetId="why-it-feels-different"
          label="why this guide feels different"
        />
        <h2>Why it feels different</h2><p>
          The experience prioritizes the current month and week, direct dos and
          don’ts, concrete examples and a clear urgent-help path. It does not
          ask readers to assemble an answer from external articles.
        </p>
      </section><section
        class="content-section"
        id="how-to-use-it-safely"
        data-share-target
        tabindex="-1"
      >
        <ShareAnchor
          targetId="how-to-use-it-safely"
          label="how to use this guide safely"
        />
        <h2>How to use it safely</h2><p>
          Use the site as a general pregnancy baseline and a way to prepare
          questions. Your doctor or midwife should guide decisions that depend
          on your health, medicines, symptoms or pregnancy, and urgent symptoms
          should never wait for a webpage.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
